      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the number of four-digit odd numbers, we need to consider the possible digits in each place. The units digit can only be 1, 3, 5, or 7 because that digit is odd. The other three digits can be any digit from 0 to 9.\n\nThe number of choices for each place is as follows:\n\n- Units digit: 4 choices\n- Thousands digit: 9 choices (since the thousands digit cannot be 0, we have 9 options)\n- Hundreds digit: 10 choices\n- Tens digit: 10 choices\n\nSo there are:\n$A = 4 \\times 9 \\times 10 \\times 10 = 3600$ four-digit odd numbers.\n\nTo find the number of four-digit multiples of 5, the last digit must be either 0 or 5. Also, the thousands digit can be any digit from 1 to 9 (since the number is four digits long and 0 cannot be the first digit), and the other three digits can be any digit from 0 to 9.\n\nThe number of choices for each place is:\n\n- Thousands digit: 9 choices\n- Units digit: 2 choices (0 or 5)\n- Hundreds digit: 10 choices\n- Tens digit: 10 choices\n\nSo there are:\n$B = 9 \\times 10 \\times 10 \\times 2 = 1800$ four-digit multiples of 5.\n\nThe sum of the number of four-digit odd numbers and four-digit multiples of 5 is $A + B = 3600 + 1800 = \\boxed{5400}$.\nThe answer is: 5400",
